  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec. 1: TCA 55-3-210 rewritten: a brand on the certificate of title for a flood motor vehicle.\n(other) Sec. 2: cross-reference in 55-3-211 changed from 55-3-209 to 55-3-210.\n(other) Sec. 3: takes effect July 1, 2011.\n(other) version: Draft 182874 (2011-02-17): flood vehicle title brand shell bill; no ID or citizenship text.\n(other) version: Draft 235152 (2011-04-06): same operative text; sponsor line changed from Tracy to Ketron.\n(other) version: Draft 513986 (2011-12-14): identical to 235152.\n(other) version: No amended, engrossed, enrolled or chaptered text, and no text of SA0296, is saved.\n(other) note: ENACTED TEXT MISSING. All three saved texts are the filed shell about flood vehicle title brands in Title 55 and carry no ID text. The official summary says the enacted bill gives a free photo ID licence to a registered voter who signs an affidavit saying they lack government photo ID and need it for voting (slot b); that rests on LegiScan's summary only. The amendments (committee amendments and SA0296) that rewrote the bill are not saved, so no quote is possible. Two roll calls on 4/20/2011 (70445 and 81075) have the same date and tally.",
